# Rotisserie Elemental: "Whenever this creature deals combat damage to a player, put a skewer counter on this creature. Then you may
# sacrifice it. If you do, exile the top X cards of your library, where X is the number of skewer counters on this creature. You may
# play those cards this turn." On turn 3 Bot1 declines the sacrifice: one counter, the Elemental stays. On turn 5 the second
# counter goes on and Bot1 accepts: the Elemental is sacrificed and exactly two cards, the Mountain and Lightning Bolt from the
# top of Bot1's own library (not the Mountain of Bot2's), are exiled. Bot1 plays the Mountain as the turn's land drop and does not
# cast the Bolt, which is no longer castable once the turn has ended: on turn 7 even with a Mox's red mana to pay it is refused.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Rotisserie Elemental
Island x5
Island
Island
Mountain
Lightning Bolt
Island x9

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain x20

